Now, a small file of marks is written so the report has something to read.
write "name,score" in "grades.csv".
add "ann,82" in "grades.csv".
add "bob,95" in "grades.csv".
add "cy,67" in "grades.csv".
add "dee,95" in "grades.csv".
add "eli,74" in "grades.csv".
add "ann,90" in "grades.csv".
add "bob,88" in "grades.csv".
add "cy,71" in "grades.csv".

Create average(xs),
    give Total(xs) / Counted(xs)!

Create with_mark(book, who, mark),
    Now, a Do cannot change data outside it, so this copies the Book and gives the new one back.
    A marks holds [mark].
    if who in book, marks holds book[who].
    if who in book, append(marks, mark).
    An out holds book.
    out[who] holds marks.
    give out!

Create load_scores(file),
    Book-of scores.
    for every row in lines(file), A p holds split(row, ","), if p:0 is not "name", scores holds Do with_mark(scores, p:0, number(p:1)).
    give scores!

Create averages(scores),
    Book-of out.
    for every who in scores, out[who] holds round(Do average(scores[who]), 1).
    give out!

Create best(avgs, skip),
    Now, finding the top student who is not ranked yet.
    A top holds nil.
    A top_score holds -1.
    for every who in avgs, if not who in skip and avgs[who] is bigger-than top_score, top holds who, top_score holds avgs[who].
    give top!

Create print_ranking(avgs),
    Now, ranking with a loop that runs once for every student.
    List-of used.
    for every place in range(Counted(avgs)), A who holds Do best(avgs, used), append(used, who), say("{place}. {who}  {avgs[who]}").
    give nil!

Create summary(scores, avgs),
    Book-of out.
    List-of values.
    A marks holds 0.
    for every who in avgs, append(values, avgs[who]), marks holds marks + Counted(scores[who]).
    List-of order holds Order(values, backward).
    out["students"] holds Counted(avgs).
    out["marks entered"] holds marks.
    out["class average"] holds round(Total(avgs) / Counted(avgs), 1).
    out["highest"] holds Bigger(avgs).
    out["lowest"] holds Smaller(avgs).
    out["all averages"] holds order.
    give out!

Create report(file),
    if not exists(file), say("There is no file called {file}"), give nil.
    A scores holds Do load_scores(file).
    An avgs holds Do averages(scores).
    say("Report for {file}").
    say("--------------------").
    Do print_ranking(avgs).
    say("--------------------").
    A stats holds Do summary(scores, avgs).
    for every k in stats, say("{k}: {stats[k]}").
    give stats!

Now, the report runs on the file above, and then on a file that is missing.
Next, a way to sort a Book by its values would replace best and print_ranking.
A result holds Do report("grades.csv").
say(Counted(result)).
Do report("missing.csv").
